# ARK Surface Rules

ARK-SMS is one Laravel runtime. Product-wise there are **three applications** — not separate customer "website" and "portal" products.

## Three applications

| Application | Routes | Views | Audience |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Customer Application** | `/`, `public.*`, `portal.*` | `resources/views/public/`, `resources/views/portal/` | Customers — anonymous and authenticated states |
| **Operations Application** | `/app/*` | `resources/views/operations/` | Staff |
| **Admin Platform** | Settings, Growth, Voice, infrastructure | Mixed under operations settings / platform | Owners / admins — not customer-facing |

Do not invent a fourth application.

**Customer application:** one product, two auth states. Sign in unlocks capability — same shell, same design system. See [ark-website-doctrine.mdc](ark-website-doctrine.mdc).

**Customer shell:** `x-customer.shell` only. `x-portal.app` and `x-public.lead-intake` delegate to it.

## Runtime

Runtime owns infrastructure only: auth, sessions, permissions, notifications, media, routing, and shared framework concerns.

Do not put operational or customer workflow ownership into runtime infrastructure.

## Operations Application

Staff/internal surface under `/app/*`.

Optimize for speed, keyboard use, density, rapid interaction, and shop workflow rhythm.

Examples: queue, RO workspace, estimates, inspections, invoicing, customer search.

## Admin Platform

Infrastructure, Growth, Voice, Settings, configuration — owner/admin surfaces that are not the customer application.

Not a separate deployable product; grouped here so engineers do not confuse platform config with customer UX.

## Layout direction

| Application | Layout |
| --- | --- |
| Customer | `resources/views/components/customer/shell.blade.php` |
| Operations | `resources/views/components/operations/app.blade.php` |

Do not build one conditional mega-layout across applications.

## Routing direction

- `routes/web.php` — public customer routes
- `routes/portal.php` — authenticated customer routes (internal name; customer UI says Sign In / My Account)
- `routes/operations.php` — staff `/app/*`

## Auth direction

- Staff: Breeze under `/app/login`, `web` guard
- Customer: `portal` guard — sign-in flow, not "portal login" in UI copy

Prefer separate staff and customer guards. Do not build one mega-user system or enterprise RBAC early.

## Do Not

- Do not split into two Laravel apps for customer vs staff.
- Do not treat customer anonymous and authenticated as separate websites.
- Do not use "Portal" in customer-facing UI.
- Do not introduce CMS frontend/admin backend assumptions.
- Do not create SaaS portal abstractions.
- Do not use SPA duplication or API-first architecture unless an operational need exists.
